  "rationale": "The batch shows a recurring structural gap: the model assigns almost no mass to paragraph breaks after an opening noun phrase or after an action sentence, while the very large generic period-after-noun rule can overwhelm other continuations. Add reusable noun-phrase patterns for opening descriptions and an action-clause-plus-punctuation pattern for paragraph breaks; add a corresponding action-clause period rule and reduce, rather than remove, the broad period-after-noun evidence. A period after an action clause can also be terminal, so the paragraph-break rule is deliberately moderate and preserves the existing end-token alternative. These patterns may still overgeneralize to unusual noun phrases or action clauses; the replay gate should check both that risk and the impact of the weight reduction."
